### 1. Fresh database (cds deploy recreates the tables, so no old runs)
$ cds deploy 2>&1 | grep deployed
/> successfully deployed to db.sqlite 

### 2. Start the server and remember its PID (server log goes to $LOG)
$ node_modules/.bin/cds-serve > $LOG 2>&1 & SERVER_PID=$!; wait_up; echo "server pid $SERVER_PID"
server pid 59131

### 3. Start an intake run for fixture D01 in the background (3 model calls: extract, classify, draft_response)
$ TEXT=$(jq -r ".[] | select(.id==\"D01\") | .text" fixtures/requests.json); echo "$TEXT"
Name: Oliver Grant
Location: Plant 1
Affected system: Windows login
Description: Back from holiday and I forgot my password. After a few tries it says the account is locked.
$ curl -sS -X POST $BASE/runIntake -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "$(jq -n --arg t "$TEXT" "{text:\$t}")" > /dev/null & CLIENT_PID=$!

### 4. As soon as the checkpoint after lookup_context is written, kill the server with SIGKILL (classify is now in flight)
$ until grep -q "next=classify" $LOG; do sleep 0.05; done; kill -9 $SERVER_PID; echo "sent SIGKILL to $SERVER_PID"
